.Dd Nov 11, 2026
.Dt KRONOS 1
.Os fauzymadani.github.io
.Sh NAME
.Nm kronos
.Nd offline timetable, task, and exam manager for Android
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a private, offline\-first Android application that keeps a class
timetable, assignments, and exams in one place.
There is no account, backend, or network permission; everything is stored in a
local SQLite database on the device.
The application id is
.Ql io.github.fauzymadani.kronos .
Debug builds append
.Ql .debug
to the id and carry a
.Ql \-debug
version suffix, so a debug and a release build install side by side.
.Pp
Devices must run Android 8.0 (API 26) or newer.
The app compiles against API 36.1 and targets API 35, and uses flat native
views rather than a declarative toolkit in order to stay responsive on
low\-end hardware.
.Sh FEATURES
.Ss Subjects
Subjects are created once, with an optional code and color, and are referenced
by timetable entries, tasks, and exams.
Subject names are unique and compared case\-insensitively after trimming.
.Ss Timetable
Class sessions carry a subject, day of week, start and end time, room,
teacher, and week number.
The timetable repeats over a rotation cycle of one to four weeks, anchored to
the semester start date, so an odd and an even week can hold different
sessions in the same slot.
Sessions can be created quickly from configured class periods, which are
named start and end time pairs edited in Settings.
Views are available per week, per day, and per month.
.Ss Tasks
Tasks carry a title, due date, optional due time, priority, category, notes,
lead time, and completion status.
Completed tasks keep a completion timestamp rather than being deleted.
Assignment type distinguishes homework from other work.
.Ss Exams
Exams carry a subject, date, start and end time, room, seat, and notes.
They are shown in a month calendar with per\-day cells, and optionally inside
the timetable day view.
.Ss Reminders
Class, task, and exam reminders are delivered through the Android
.Ql AlarmManager
with notification channels, and require notification permission on the device.
Only the next relevant boundary is scheduled; nothing polls in the background.
Pending alarms are rebuilt after boot, a time change, or a timezone change.
.Ss Home screen widget
A timetable widget shows the current or next classes.
It never polls: the update period is zero, and it refreshes when data changes
or when the next class boundary passes.
.Ss Backup, restore, and CSV export
Backup writes a JSON file containing subjects, sessions, tasks, categories,
exams, holidays, and settings, and restoring replaces local data from that file.
The accent color is deliberately excluded, because a backup brought to another
phone should not repaint that phone.
Timetable data can also be exported as CSV for use elsewhere.
.Ss Appearance
The interface supports light, dark, battery\-saving automatic, and pure black
modes, seven accent colors, twelve and twenty\-four hour time formats, and a
Monday or Sunday week start.
The user interface is English and Indonesian.
.Sh SETTINGS
Settings are kept in shared preferences and are reachable from the Settings
screen, which has a back arrow returning to the previous screen.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm theme_mode
One of
.Ql light ,
.Ql dark ,
or
.Ql auto_battery ,
the last following the system battery saver.
.It Cm pure_black
Use an absolute black background in dark mode, for OLED panels.
.It Cm accent_color
One of the built\-in accent swatches; device-local and not exported.
.It Cm time_format
.Ql 24
or
.Ql 12 .
.It Cm first_day_of_week
.Ql monday
or
.Ql sunday .
.It Cm rotation_length
Rotation cycle in weeks, one to four.
.It Cm semester_start
Anchor date for week numbering.
.It Cm class_periods
Named period start and end times, used as presets in the class editor.
.It Cm default_reminder_offset
Default reminder lead time in minutes.
.It Cm class_reminders , task_reminders , exam_reminders
Per\-category reminder switches.
.It Cm exam_day_before , exam_hour_before
Optional early exam warnings.
.It Cm exam_reminder_hour
Time of day at which the day\-before exam warning fires.
.It Cm day_view_exams
Show exams inside the timetable day view.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev ANDROID_HOME , Ev ANDROID_SDK_ROOT
Android SDK location.
Either one takes precedence over
.Pa local.properties .
.It Ev BUILD_TOOLS
Overrides the automatically detected build\-tools version for
.Ql make apk\-info .
.It Ev AVD
Emulator name for
.Ql make boot ;
defaults to the first available emulator.
.It Ev JAVA_HOME
JDK 17, required to build.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /data/data/io.github.fauzymadani.kronos/databases/kronos.db
Room database, the single source of truth for application data.
The schema is at version 10; versions 1 through 10 are upgraded by explicit
migrations and there is no destructive fallback, so an older build cannot open
a newer database.
.It Pa /data/data/io.github.fauzymadani.kronos/shared_prefs/kronos_settings.xml
Preferences described under
.Sx SETTINGS .
.It Pa app/schemas
Exported Room schemas, committed so migrations can be reviewed and tested.
.It Pa app/src/main/res/raw/license.txt
License text shown in the About dialog.
.It Pa keystore.properties
Signing material for the release build.
When absent, the release build falls back to the debug signing configuration.
Never committed.
.It Pa local.properties
Local SDK location, generated by the IDE and never committed.
When
.Ev ANDROID_HOME
is unset, the
.Pa Makefile
reads the SDK path from this file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build and run a debug build, which includes LeakCanary and is not minified:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make build
make install
make logcat
.Ed
.Pp
Run the unit tests:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make test
.Ed
.Pp
Build a minified release and update an existing install in place.
.Ql adb install \-r
keeps application data, and the version code must not decrease:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make install\-release
.Ed
.Pp
Confirm the version in the installed package and in the built artifact:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make version
make apk\-info
.Ed
.Pp
Read this manual from the repository:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
man \-l kronos.1
.Ed
.Pp
Install it for
.Ql man kronos :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
install \-m 644 kronos.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Ql make logcat
follows logcat for the application process, and
.Ql make crash
prints the crash buffer.
.Ql make version
prints the installed version, and
.Ql make apk\-info
prints the version and signing certificate of the built release APK.
.Pp
Debug builds include LeakCanary.
Reports pointing at
.Ql DecorView
or
.Ql InputMethodManager
originate inside the library rather than in application code.
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
Android 8.0 (API 26) and newer, with the interface localised in English and
Indonesian.
Release builds are minified and resource\-shrunk by R8; an update that behaves
differently from a debug build points at
.Pa app/proguard-rules.pro .
